   </table><p style="text-indent:6.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The Compensation Committee reviewed the Company&#8217;s performance against the pre-established 2024 CFO Performance Objectives shortly following each quarterly-performance period for 2024. The Compensation Committee determined that the non-GAAP operating expense target was satisfied for all four quarters during 2024 and that the cash balance target was not satisfied for the first or second quarter of 2024 but had been achieved for the third and fourth quarters of 2024.  Accordingly, our Chief Financial Officer earned and was paid a cash bonus of $15,625 for each of the first and second quarters and a cash bonus of $31,250 for each of the third and fourth quarters.</span></p><p style="text-indent:6.667%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">For 2024, our former Chief Executive Officer was eligible to earn a performance bonus of up to up to $100,000 each quarter, entirely in the form of common stock of the Company, except for amounts withheld in cash to cover taxes and other voluntary and involuntary payroll deductions and withholdings. The Compensation Committee established quarterly performance objectives for revenue and net income, as determined in accordance with U.S. GAAP, for our former Chief Executive Officer as follows (the &#8220;2024 Former CEO Performance Objectives&#8221;):</span></p>
   <table style="margin-left:auto;border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:100.0%;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;">
    <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
     <td style="width:60.2%;box-sizing:content-box;"/>
